From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] venus: Vulkan on Windows over the viogpu3d kernel driver

Venus (Mesa's Vulkan driver for virtio-gpu) only ran on Linux, over the DRM
ioctls. Port it to Windows on top of the viogpu3d kernel driver's escapes:

- vn_renderer_wddm.c: a renderer for the viogpu3d driver. It finds the
  virtio-gpu adapter among all adapters (in an RDP session the desktop's
  adapter is a remote one), creates a D3DKMT device that carries the Venus
  context, and uses the escapes VIOGPU_GET_CAPS and VIOGPU_CTX_INIT, then
  VIOGPU_BLOB_CREATE/MAP/DESTROY for shared memory and host-visible device
  memory and VIOGPU_EXECBUFFER for command streams. Renderer syncs are
  emulated with the event the driver sets when a ring's fence signals, the
  way vn_renderer_virtgpu.c emulates drm_syncobjs with sync files; there are
  no external memory or syncs, so no fd-based extensions are offered.
- The escapes' structures in viogpu_wddm_driver.h (same as the driver's).
- Win32 WSI on its software path: the GPU copies each frame to host-visible
  memory and GDI draws it into the window (the DXGI path needs a D3D12
  queue). VK_KHR_win32_surface and the swapchain extensions are offered
  without external memory.
- Windows stand-ins: thread ids, no sync files, no Linux nice value for the
  ring priority, QueryPerformanceCounter for calibrated timestamps, and a
  types-only branch in drm-uapi/drm.h (drm_fourcc.h needs the types).
- Build: venus builds on Windows with clang-cl (it needs C11 atomics and
  typeof, which MSVC 14.38 lacks). u_atomic.h uses the GCC builtins with
  clang-cl (its intrin.h lacks the lowercase _interlocked* names); the
  version-script, dynamic-list and -Bsymbolic checks are skipped for
  MSVC-style compilers (clang-cl hands -Wl, options to lld-link, which took
  the map for an input file); src/virtio is built for a Vulkan-only build;
  the DirectX headers (Win32 WSI includes directx/d3d12.h) come in for any
  Vulkan driver on Windows; the DLL exports through vulkan_api.def, and its
  manifest names the DLL next to it, both named by the new
  vulkan-virtio-dll-name option.

Tested on the RTX 3080 host through vhost-user-gpu (WinBoat's image 6.05-8):
memory, compute, rendering, texture sampling, timeline semaphores and a
swapchain, 64- and 32-bit (WinBoat's DirectX test, groups vulkan and
vulkan-32).
---
---
